{"id":2,"title":"Fractions — Fundamentals","subject":"algebra","sections":[{"id":"fraction-basics","title":"1 · What a fraction means","kind":"learn","steps":[{"kind":"video","id":"fraction-basics","minutes":6.1,"title":"What Is a Fraction?"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-076","stem":"\\(\\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{?}{24}\\)","choices":["\\(20\\)","\\(18\\)","\\(16\\)","\\(12\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["The denominator went from 4 to 24 — multiplied by 6. So multiply the numerator by 6 as well: 3 · 6 = 18 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-077","stem":"\\(\\frac{60}{240} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["240 : 60 = 4 , so 60 fits into 240 exactly four times: 60:240 = 1:4 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-078","stem":"\\(\\frac{6}{15} = \\frac{?}{10}\\)","choices":["\\(5\\)","\\(4\\)","\\(3\\)","\\(6\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Reduce first: 6:15 = 2:5 . Then expand to tenths: 2:5 = 4:10 , so the missing numerator is 4."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-079","stem":"\\(\\frac{29}{6} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(4\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\)","\\(5\\,\\frac{1}{6}\\)","\\(4\\,\\frac{5}{6}\\)","\\(5\\,\\frac{5}{6}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["29 : 6 = 4 remainder 5, so 29:6 = 4 5:6 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-080","stem":"\\(7\\,\\frac{2}{5} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{37}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{39}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{35}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{36}{5}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Mixed to improper: 7 · 5 + 2 = 37 , so 7 2:5 = 37:5 ."]}]},{"id":"fraction-multiply","title":"2 · Multiplying and dividing","kind":"learn","steps":[{"kind":"video","id":"fraction-multiply","minutes":5.4,"title":"Multiplying & Dividing Fractions"},{"kind":"question","id":"q-071","stem":"\\(\\frac{6}{12} \\cdot  \\frac{2}{8} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Reduce each factor first: 6:12 = 1:2 and 2:8 = 1:4 . Then 1:2 · 1:4 = 1:8 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-072","stem":"\\(\\frac{15}{14} \\cdot  4\\,\\frac{2}{3} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(7\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(4\\)","\\(6\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Convert: 4 2:3 = 14:3 . Then 15:14 · 14:3 — the fourteens cancel — leaving 15:3 = 5 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-073","stem":"\\(\\frac{7}{12} :  \\frac{1}{3} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(1\\,\\frac{3}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{7}{36}\\)","\\(\\frac{4}{7}\\)","\\(1\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Flip and multiply: 7:12 · 3:1 = 21:12 = 7:4 = 1 3:4 . The distractor 7:36 comes from multiplying by 1:3 without flipping."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-074","stem":"\\(\\frac{\\frac{7}{5}}{\\frac{3}{5}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(2\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\)","\\(1\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\)","\\(1\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Flip and multiply: 7:5 · 5:3 — the fives cancel — leaving 7:3 = 2 1:3 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-075","stem":"\\(8 :  3\\,\\frac{1}{5} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(1\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{2}{5}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Convert: 3 1:5 = 16:5 . Then 8 : 16:5 = 8 · 5:16 = 40:16 = 5:2 = 2 1:2 ."]}]},{"id":"fraction-add","title":"3 · Adding and subtracting","kind":"learn","steps":[{"kind":"video","id":"fraction-add","minutes":3.7,"title":"Adding & Subtracting Fractions"},{"kind":"card","id":"mem-fractions","title":"Fraction rules","intro":"Name the operation first — then use its rule.","tables":[{"title":"","head":["Operation","Rule","Example"],"rows":[["Add / subtract","common denominator, then add or subtract the tops","\\(\\frac38+\\frac5{12}=\\frac9{24}+\\frac{10}{24}=\\frac{19}{24}\\)"],["Multiply","top × top, bottom × bottom (cancel first)","\\(\\frac{14}{15}\\cdot\\frac{25}{21}=\\frac{10}{9}\\)"],["Divide","multiply by the reciprocal of the second","\\(\\frac34:\\frac25=\\frac34\\cdot\\frac52=\\frac{15}8\\)"],["Mixed → improper","whole × denominator + numerator, same denominator","\\(2\\frac35=\\frac{13}5\\)"],["Improper → mixed","how many times it fits; remainder on top","\\(\\frac{15}4=3\\frac34\\)"],["Expand / reduce","same factor on top and bottom","\\(\\frac{18}{24}=\\frac34\\)"]]}],"tips":["Bigger numerator → bigger fraction. Bigger denominator → smaller fraction.","Cancel factors only — never a term inside a sum."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-066","stem":"\\(\\frac{3}{8} + \\frac{2}{8} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{5}{16}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{5}{8}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Same denominators: add the numerators and keep the denominator: 3:8 + 2:8 = 5:8 . The distractor 5:16 comes from also adding the denominators."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-067","stem":"\\(\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{3}{8} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{8}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Convert to eighths: 1:2 = 4:8 . Then 4:8 − 3:8 = 1:8 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-068","stem":"\\(\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{5} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{15}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{8}{15}\\)","\\(\\frac{7}{15}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["LCM(3, 5) = 15 : 1:3 = 5:15 and 1:5 = 3:15 , so the sum is 5:15 + 3:15 = 8:15 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-069","stem":"\\(4\\,\\frac{2}{3} - 2\\,\\frac{1}{4} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(2\\,\\frac{5}{12}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{1}{12}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{7}{12}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Convert: 4 2:3 = 14:3 and 2 1:4 = 9:4 . With denominator 12: 56:12 − 27:12 = 29:12 = 2 5:12 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-070","stem":"\\(\\frac{2}{5} - \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{7}{10} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(1\\)","\\(\\frac{9}{10}\\)","\\(1\\,\\frac{1}{10}\\)","\\(\\frac{4}{5}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Convert to tenths: 2:5 = 4:10 . Then 4:10 − 1:10 + 7:10 = 10:10 = 1 ."]}]},{"id":"decimals","title":"4 · Decimal fractions","kind":"learn","steps":[{"kind":"video","id":"decimals","minutes":6.6,"title":"Decimal Fractions"},{"kind":"card","id":"mem-decimals","title":"Fractions ↔ decimals","intro":"Know these by heart — they show up everywhere.","tables":[{"title":"","head":["Fraction","Decimal","Fraction","Decimal"],"rows":[["\\(\\frac12\\)","\\(0.5\\)","\\(\\frac15\\)","\\(0.2\\)"],["\\(\\frac14\\)","\\(0.25\\)","\\(\\frac25\\)","\\(0.4\\)"],["\\(\\frac34\\)","\\(0.75\\)","\\(\\frac18\\)","\\(0.125\\)"],["\\(\\frac1{10}\\)","\\(0.1\\)","\\(\\frac38\\)","\\(0.375\\)"],["\\(\\frac1{100}\\)","\\(0.01\\)","\\(\\frac13\\)","\\(0.333\\ldots\\) (never exact)"]]},{"title":"Moving the point","head":["Operation","Point moves"],"rows":[["\\(\\times10,\\ \\times100,\\ \\times1000\\)","right: one place per zero"],["\\(:10,\\ :100,\\ :1000\\)","left: one place per zero"]]}],"tips":["Number of decimal places = number of zeros in the denominator: \\(0.37=\\frac{37}{100}\\).","Zeros at the far right change nothing: \\(0.5=0.50=0.500\\)."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-061","stem":"\\(0.45 = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{4}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{9}{20}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{45}\\)","\\(\\frac{5}{9}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["0.45 = 45:100 . Divide top and bottom by 5: 9:20 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-062","stem":"\\(\\frac{18}{25} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(0.25\\)","\\(0.18\\)","\\(0.72\\)","\\(0.36\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Expand to hundredths: 18:25 = 72:100 = 0.72 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-063","stem":"\\(12.3 - 4.15 = ?\\)","choices":["\\(8.15\\)","\\(8.25\\)","\\(8.05\\)","\\(7.85\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Write 12.3 as 12.30 and subtract with aligned points: 12.30 − 4.15 = 8.15 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-064","stem":"\\(\\frac{18}{0.6} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(3\\)","\\(30\\)","\\(12\\)","\\(6\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Multiply top and bottom by 10: 18:0.6 = 180:6 = 30 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-065","stem":"\\({\\left(0.9\\right)}^{2} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(8.1\\)","\\(0.81\\)","\\(0.081\\)","\\(81\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["0.9 · 0.9 : digits give 81; one decimal place in each factor makes two in the product: 0.81."]}]},{"id":"unit-t2-1","title":"5 · Mixed fraction practice","kind":"practice","steps":[{"kind":"question","id":"q-041","stem":"\\(\\frac{5}{6} = \\frac{35}{?}\\)","choices":["\\(48\\)","\\(36\\)","\\(42\\)","\\(40\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["The numerator went from 5 to 35 — multiplied by 7. To keep the fraction's value, multiply the denominator by 7 too: 6 · 7 = 42 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-042","stem":"\\(\\frac{4}{12} = \\frac{?}{27}\\)","choices":["\\(9\\)","\\(12\\)","\\(6\\)","\\(8\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["First reduce: 4:12 = 1:3 . Then expand 1:3 to a denominator of 27: 27 : 3 = 9 , so the numerator is 1 · 9 = 9 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-043","stem":"\\(\\frac{27}{45} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{4}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{5}{9}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["The greatest common divisor of 27 and 45 is 9. Dividing both: 27 : 9 = 3 and 45 : 9 = 5 , so 27:45 = 3:5 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-044","stem":"\\(\\frac{52}{10} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(5\\,\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(5\\,\\frac{1}{5}\\)","\\(5\\,\\frac{2}{5}\\)","\\(5\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["52 : 10 = 5 remainder 2, so 52:10 = 5 2:10 , and 2:10 reduces to 1:5 . The answer is 5 1:5 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-045","stem":"\\(7\\,\\frac{1}{6} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{45}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{43}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{37}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{41}{6}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Mixed to improper: multiply the whole part by the denominator and add the numerator: 7 · 6 + 1 = 43 , so 7 1:6 = 43:6 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-046","stem":"\\(\\frac{6}{15} \\cdot  \\frac{5}{8} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Reduce before multiplying: 6:15 = 2:5 . Then 2:5 · 5:8 — the fives cancel — leaving 2:8 = 1:4 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-047","stem":"\\(2\\,\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot  \\frac{7}{35} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Convert the mixed number: 2 1:2 = 5:2 . Then 5:2 · 7:35 = 35:70 = 1:2 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-048","stem":"\\(\\frac{6}{25} :  \\frac{9}{5} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{2}{15}\\)","\\(\\frac{54}{125}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{15}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal: 6:25 · 5:9 = 30:225 = 2:15 . The distractor 54:125 comes from multiplying without flipping."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-049","stem":"\\(\\frac{\\frac{2}{9}}{\\frac{8}{3}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{16}{27}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{12}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["A fraction over a fraction is division: 2:9 : 8:3 = 2:9 · 3:8 = 6:72 = 1:12 . The distractor 16:27 comes from multiplying instead of dividing."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-050","stem":"\\(\\frac{4}{\\frac{1}{8}} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(16\\)","\\(32\\)","\\(8\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Dividing by 1:8 is multiplying by 8: 4 · 8 = 32 . The distractor 1:2 comes from multiplying by 1:8 instead of its reciprocal."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-051","stem":"\\(\\frac{1}{4} + \\frac{3}{8} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{5}{8}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{32}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)","\\(\\frac{7}{8}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Common denominator 8: 1:4 = 2:8 , so 2:8 + 3:8 = 5:8 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-052","stem":"\\(\\frac{5}{9} - \\frac{1}{3} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{9}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{9}\\)","\\(\\frac{4}{9}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Common denominator 9: 1:3 = 3:9 , so 5:9 − 3:9 = 2:9 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-053","stem":"\\(\\frac{5}{18} + \\frac{7}{12} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{27}{32}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{5}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{31}{36}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["LCM(18, 12) = 36 : 5:18 = 10:36 and 7:12 = 21:36 , so the sum is 10:36 + 21:36 = 31:36 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-054","stem":"\\(3\\,\\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{7}{9} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(2\\,\\frac{17}{36}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{5}{13}\\)","\\(2\\,\\frac{19}{36}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Convert: 3 1:4 = 13:4 . With LCM(4, 9) = 36 : 13:4 = 117:36 and 7:9 = 28:36 . Subtract: (117 − 28):36 = 89:36 = 2 17:36 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-055","stem":"\\(\\frac{7}{20} + \\frac{3}{4} - \\frac{3}{5} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["LCM(20, 4, 5) = 20 : 3:4 = 15:20 and 3:5 = 12:20 . Then 7:20 + 15:20 − 12:20 = 10:20 = 1:2 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-056","stem":"\\(0.250 = ?\\)","choices":["\\(\\frac{1}{25}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{250}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"],"correct":3,"explanation":["The trailing zero changes nothing: 0.250 = 0.25 = 25:100 = 1:4 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-057","stem":"\\(\\frac{6}{120} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(0.05\\)","\\(0.06\\)","\\(0.5\\)","\\(0.02\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Reduce first: 6:120 = 1:20 . Then 1:20 = 5:100 = 0.05 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-058","stem":"\\(30.25 - 8.85 = ?\\)","choices":["\\(21.3\\)","\\(21.4\\)","\\(22.4\\)","\\(22.3\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Compensate: 8.85 is 0.15 short of 9. Subtract 9 to get 21.25, then add back 0.15: 21.25 + 0.15 = 21.40 = 21.4 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-059","stem":"\\(\\frac{12}{1.5} = ?\\)","choices":["\\(6\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(9\\)","\\(7\\)"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Clear the decimal by multiplying top and bottom by 10: 12:1.5 = 120:15 = 8 ."]},{"kind":"question","id":"q-060","stem":"\\(0.3 \\cdot  0.6 = ?\\)","choices":["\\(0.18\\)","\\(1.8\\)","\\(0.018\\)","\\(0.108\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Multiply the digits: 3 · 6 = 18 . Count decimal places: one in each factor, two in total, so place the point two digits in: 0.18."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t2-1-1","stem":"Evaluate \\(\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac14\\).","choices":["\\(\\frac{3}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)","\\(1\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["The first fraction simplifies to one half. Two quarters plus one quarter is three quarters."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t2-1-2","stem":"Evaluate \\(\\frac56-\\frac14\\).","choices":["\\(\\frac{7}{12}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Use twelfths: ten twelfths minus three twelfths gives seven twelfths."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t2-1-3","stem":"Evaluate \\(\\frac{9}7\\times\\frac{14}{3}\\).","choices":["12","6","3","7"],"correct":1,"explanation":["Cancel 3 across the factors and cancel seven into fourteen. The remaining factors are three and two."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t2-1-4","stem":"Evaluate \\(\\frac34:\\frac9{10}\\).","choices":["\\(\\frac{5}{6}\\)","\\(\\frac{27}{40}\\)","\\(\\frac{6}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{2}{3}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Multiply by the reciprocal of nine tenths, then cancel three into nine and ten with four."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t2-1-5","stem":"What fraction equals 0.375?","choices":["\\(\\frac{3}{8}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{37}{100}\\)","\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\)"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Write 375 thousandths and divide numerator and denominator by 125."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t2-1-6","stem":"A ribbon is \\(\\frac{7}2\\) meters long. It is cut into pieces of \\(\\frac12\\) meter with no waste. How many pieces are made?","choices":["7","6","8","3"],"correct":0,"explanation":["Divide the total length by one half, which doubles it."]},{"kind":"question","id":"alg-extra-unit-t2-1-7","stem":"Which fraction is the reciprocal of \\(-\\frac{3}{5}\\)?","choices":["\\(-\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(\\frac{3}{5}\\)","\\(-\\frac{5}{3}\\)","\\(\\frac{5}{3}\\)"],"correct":2,"explanation":["Swap numerator and denominator and keep the negative sign."]}]}],"passages":{}}